The 874,227 replacement characters in each of the four original control logs come from the original bare `git show` diagnostic, before the test-output marker. A fresh read-only execution of that command in each frozen image reproduced the bytes exactly. All four test-output regions decode as UTF-8 without replacements. No Docker multiplex framing or archive transport contamination was observed.

This behavior exposes a source-history difference in the ARM port: its source checkout contains the exact base commit fetched with `--depth=1`, while the published Dockerfile clones repository history. In a shallow checkout, the diagnostic displays a root-commit diff containing binary data. This difference remains part of the environment identity. It did not alter the designated test region or the native grading input within that region. The native upstream decoder's `errors="replace"` behavior remains appropriate; the original results are preserved without a scoring correction.

The first structural classifier's `eval_has_python_diagnostic_block` field was an overly broad command-presence heuristic. It did not establish the byte origin. The later byte-for-byte reproduction supersedes that inference. Likewise, the first supplementary comparison incorrectly reused the 6028 reproduction for the distinct 5414 source commit; its failed assertion and script snapshot are retained. The final audit uses each image's own reproduction.

[The supplementary audit](encoding_audit_v2.json) records all four raw-log hashes, exact reproduction offsets, byte counts and UTF-8 checks without revealing test names or contents. [The auditor](encoding_audit_v2.py) performs only read-only custody comparisons. These files supplement the original immutable artifact inventory; the original report, receipts and checksums remain unchanged. No model inference was performed.
